Preface

Ps 127:3 says, ‘Behold, children are a heritage from the
Lord, the fruit of the womb is a reward’ (NKJV). In other
words, your children are God’s property and He gifts them
to you as a reward based on His trust in you to raise them
for Him. The ultimate proof of responsibility is that you
raise them to become all God wants them to be and to
fulfil the purpose and destiny that God has for them. One
spiritual strategy to apply bringing up children is to daily
declare God’s word over them. This should start from
conception, when you lay hands on the child in the womb
and prophesy over them, to childhood when you lay
hands on their heads and decrees words over them.
Ultimately when the children are grown and are on their
own, you can still send these prophecies of scriptures to
them wherever they are. Since there is no distance in the
realm of the spirit, you can parent them prophetically by
charting their life courses with your words irrespective of
where they are. Remember, parenting is a lifetime task.

These prophetic confessions when made consistently and
effectively will be an invisible compass that will guide
your children to becoming all that God has called them to
be and also help them fulfill purpose. Do well to find a
suitable atmosphere and engage effectively, routinely and
continually. It takes time for the things of the spirit to
crystalise, so these meditations will become tangible in
their lives after a length of time of use.
